// motion-master.jsonc — auto-loaded config bundled with the Windows release.
//
// Motion Master auto-loads a "motion-master.jsonc" placed next to the executable — no --config
// needed (an explicit --config, if given, overrides this file). This file ships in the Windows
// package to raise the real-time cycle period to 4 ms, which most stock Windows systems can sustain
// reliably: the 1 ms built-in default overruns on typical Windows timer granularity (~1.5 ms), so
// the loop degrades to skip-to-grid and drops cycles. 4 ms leaves comfortable headroom.
//
// Every other setting keeps its built-in default — see the fully annotated motion-master.example.jsonc
// alongside this file for the complete list. This is JSONC: // and /* */ comments are allowed.
{
  // Real-time cyclic loop.
  "gameLoop": {
    "periodUs": 4000  // 4 ms — robust on stock Windows; the built-in default is 1000 (1 ms)
  }
}
